From 2bde5e8fa6f17dabf36cc4f66cd3531b23fdcc3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ismael Oliva <isma.oliva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:20:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gugu: session/fork via pi --fork

Why: Gugu's side chat and fork task on the chat (ACP) leg fork through
session/fork; pi-acp does not advertise sessionCapabilities.fork, so Pi
had no fork on that leg although the pi CLI can fork (pi --fork). This
is upstream PR #171 as proposed: the adapter starts pi with
--fork <source file> --session-id <new id>, pi copies the file before
extensions load, and the forking process keeps serving the fork for the
client's first session/load.

Upstream: svkozak/pi-acp#171 (by Ismael Oliva).

Drop when: upstream releases session/fork.
---
